 while EBITDA rose two hundred fifty-six percent to seven hundred thirty crore rupees.","quote":"International Ports delivered robust growth, with revenue increasing 80% YoY to ₹1,747 Cr and EBITDA surging 256% YoY to ₹730 Cr","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/rkbhagia_29072026124451_IntimationofPRandIP.pdf","page":2.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"improved","statement":"Marine revenue rose sixty-seven percent year-over-year to nine hundred one crore rupees due to offshore vessel additions and European subsea expansion.","quote":"Marine revenue increased 67% YoY to ₹901 Cr, on the back of ongoing offshore vessel additions and European subsea expansion","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/rkbhagia_29072026124451_IntimationofPRandIP.pdf","page":2.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"deteriorated","statement":"Rail container volumes for the logistics business were negatively affected by the ongoing crisis in the Middle East.","quote":"Logistics business TEU rail volumes were impacted due to the ongoing Middle East crisis.","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/rkbhagia_29072026124451_IntimationofPRandIP.pdf","page":3.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"deteriorated","statement":"Rail volumes in TEUs decreased to one hundred forty-five thousand three hundred ten in the first quarter of fiscal year 2027 from one hundred seventy-nine thousand four hundred seventy-nine in the first quarter of fiscal year 2026.","quote":"Rail volume (TEUs) stood at 145,310 for Q1 FY27 (179,479 for Q1 FY26).","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/rkbhagia_29072026124451_IntimationofPRandIP.pdf","page":3.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"outlook","statement":"The company's domestic ports business continues to deliver strong growth and remains the bedrock of its earnings, while other segments have transitioned from scale-up to scale-value.","quote":"Our domestic ports business continued to deliver strong growth and remains the bedrock of APSEZ's earnings, while International Ports, Marine, and Logistics have transitioned decisively from scale-up to scale-value","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/rkbhagia_29072026124451_IntimationofPRandIP.pdf","page":2.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"outlook","statement":"The company's balanced growth across its various business segments increases its confidence in reaching its Ambition 2031 targets.","quote":"This balanced growth across businesses reinforces our confidence in achieving Ambition 2031.","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/rkbhagia_29072026124451_IntimationofPRandIP.pdf","page":2.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"guidance","statement":"Adani Ports is executing a major port capacity expansion program to increase domestic capacity to one thousand million metric tonnes by December 2030.","quote":"APSEZ is undertaking one of the largest port capacity expansion programs in its history, with domestic capacity slated to increase to 1,000 MMT by December 2030, laying the foundation for the next phase of growth.","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/rkbhagia_29072026124451_IntimationofPRandIP.pdf","page":3.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"guidance","statement":"The company has reaffirmed its long-term climate goal by committing to achieve Net Zero emissions by the year 2040.","quote":"Reaffirmed long term climate ambition with a Net Zero commitment by 2040","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/rkbhagia_29072026124451_IntimationofPRandIP.pdf","page":30.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"demand","statement":"The company directly benefits from India's gross domestic product growth, which is driven by industrialization, infrastructure, energy, and agriculture.","quote":"Direct beneficiary of India’s GDP growth led by: Industrialization Infrastructure Energy Agriculture","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/rkbhagia_29072026124451_IntimationofPRandIP.pdf","page":8.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"demand","statement":"Cargo volumes are expected to be boosted by China plus one manufacturing capital expenditure, recently signed free trade agreements, and the development of the India, Middle East, Europe Corridor.","quote":"Cargo boost via China+1 manufacturing capex, recently signed FTAs, IMEC corridor development","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/rkbhagia_29072026124451_IntimationofPRandIP.pdf","page":8.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"pricing","statement":"Revenue from domestic ports increased by twelve percent year-over-year, supported by cargo volume growth, an improved product mix, and higher realizations.","quote":"Domestic ports revenue grew 12% YoY driven by cargo volume growth (115.3 MMT in Q1 FY27 vs. 112.9 MMT in Q1FY26), superior product mix and higher realization.","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/rkbhagia_29072026124451_IntimationofPRandIP.pdf","page":3.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"margins","statement":"The domestic ports business achieved an EBITDA margin of seventy-four percent, which is considered best-in-class.","quote":"Domestic ports revenue grew 12% YoY, driven by cargo volume growth, superior product mix, and higher realization. EBITDA margin stood at a best-in-class 74%","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/rkbhagia_29072026124451_IntimationofPRandIP.pdf","page":2.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"margins","statement":"The addition of higher-margin operations in Australia and the scaling up of Colombo operations led to a significant increase in the EBITDA margin for international ports to forty-one point eight percent.","quote":"The inclusion of higher-margin Australia operations and improving scale at Colombo drove a sharp expansion in EBITDA margin to 41.8% in Q1 FY27 from 21.1% in Q1 FY26.","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/rkbhagia_29072026124451_IntimationofPRandIP.pdf","page":3.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"capex","statement":"The company plans to invest up to one hundred million dollars over two phases to speed up automation and optimization through its partnership with Kaleris.","quote":"APSEZ will invest up to $100 million in two phases to accelerate automation and optimisation through this partnership.","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/rkbhagia_29072026124451_IntimationofPRandIP.pdf","page":26.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"capacity","statement":"The capacity of domestic ports reached six hundred fifty-three million metric tonnes as of June 30, 2026, as the company undertakes a major port capacity expansion program.","quote":"As of June 30, 2026, domestic ports capacity stood at 653 MMT. APSEZ is undertaking one of the largest port capacity expansion programs in its history","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/rkbhagia_29072026124451_IntimationofPRandIP.pdf","page":3.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"capacity","statement":"The partnership with Kaleris is expected to accelerate the unlocking of ninety-one million metric tonnes of additional capacity by 2030.","quote":"This collaboration will expedite the unlocking of 91 MMT of additional capacity (~10% of installed capacity) by 2030.","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/rkbhagia_29072026124451_IntimationofPRandIP.pdf","page":26.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"orders","statement":"The company secured a ten-year marine services contract to support Argentina's initial liquefied natural gas exports to India, marking its entry into South America.","quote":"APSEZ has secured a 10-Year Marine Services contract for Argentina’s first LNG Export to India."